# WebGL: No Threads

Our builds target WebGL, which runs **single-threaded**. C# threading APIs either throw at runtime, deadlock, or silently degrade to main-thread execution. Write all code main-thread-only.

## Banned

- `new Thread(...)`, `ThreadPool.QueueUserWorkItem`
- `Task.Run(...)`, `Task.Factory.StartNew(...)`
- `Parallel.For` / `Parallel.ForEach` / PLINQ (`AsParallel`)
- `lock`, `Monitor`, `Mutex`, `SemaphoreSlim`, `Interlocked` patterns that *expect* concurrency (they compile, but they're dead weight and signal a design that assumes threads)
- Blocking waits: `Task.Wait()`, `Task.Result`, `Thread.Sleep` — these **deadlock or freeze the browser tab**; there is no other thread to complete the work
- `System.Timers.Timer` / `System.Threading.Timer` — use Unity time instead

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — deadlocks on WebGL
var data = FetchAsync().Result;
Task.Run(() => BuildGrid());

// ✅ GOOD — await on the main thread
var data = await FetchAsync();

// ✅ GOOD — heavy work time-sliced across frames instead of offloaded
private IEnumerator BuildGridSliced()
{
    for (int row = 0; row < _rows; row++)
    {
        BuildRow(row);
        yield return null;
    }
}
```

## What to use instead

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Async I/O (network, asset load) | `async`/`await` on the main thread, `UnityWebRequest`, coroutines |
| Heavy CPU work | Time-slice across frames (coroutine / amortized loop — see frame-budget rule) |
| Delays / timers | `Time.time` comparisons, coroutines, `Awaitable.WaitForSecondsAsync` |
| Parallel data crunch | C# Job System with Burst — jobs **run on the main thread** in WebGL but Burst still vectorizes; schedule and `Complete()` same frame, don't rely on overlap |

`async`/`await` itself works on WebGL (single-threaded `SynchronizationContext`) — continuations run on the main thread. That's fine; blocking on tasks is what kills you.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No `Thread`, `Task.Run`, `Parallel`, thread-pool, or timer APIs
- [ ] No `.Result` / `.Wait()` / `Thread.Sleep` blocking calls
- [ ] Heavy work time-sliced across frames, not "offloaded"
- [ ] No design that assumes background threads exist
